  "question": {
    "text": "A capillary tube is immersed vertically in water and the height of the water column is <math> <mrow> <mi></mi><mi></mi><mi></mi><mi></mi><mi></mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo> </mrow> </math>. When this arrangement is taken into a mine of depth d, the height of the water column is <math> <mrow> <mi></mi><mi></mi><mi></mi><mi></mi><mi></mi><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo> </mrow> </math>. If R is the radius of earth, the ratio <math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mi></mi><mi></mi><mi></mi><mi></mi><mi></mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo> </mrow> <mrow> <mi></mi><mi></mi><mi></mi><mi></mi><mi></mi><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;is :",
    "image": null
  },
